# Vite

Per owning package: apply only if its `package.json` has `vite` and not `next`. If both, Next wins for that package. If the owning package has no `vite`, this file is inert. Confirm before applying; globs are candidates. Do not import `next/navigation`, `next/image`, or `getServerSideProps`.

Read `vite.config.*`, the owning `package.json` (type/exports), and neighbors. Entry is `index.html` + `src/main.*` for apps; libraries and custom setups follow this config (lib mode, custom entry). Shared React packages get no app-specific assumptions.

## Hard
- Env: `import.meta.env` (`VITE_` prefix unless `envPrefix` says otherwise). Do not invent Next `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` here.
- Client SPA by default; library/custom modes per this config. No RSC, no `app/` router conventions, no Server Components.
- SSR only per this config's plugin/docs (e.g. vike); frameworks may wrap Vite with their own conventions — match them. Do not invent Next `loading.tsx`.
- Aliases and `base` come from this Vite config, not from Next `basePath`.
- Tests: Vitest when `vitest` is a dependency. Repo manager.
